I'm now one for one in the 2003 tournament, but that could be a fluke of 
the RNG.  Only took 20540 turns, my best time yet.  I actually arrived at 
the Lawful altar in just under 20k turns, but had no way to self-convert.  
So I spent 500 turns taming the riders, and then went to the correct altar.

Right now I'm the third-best priest, scoring just less than some guy who 
drowned on the Juiblex level... yeah, the nethack score system sucks.  The 
game playback files are at 
http://nethack.devnull.net/cgi-bin/tournament/playbacks.pl





I explored the first two levels of the mines, but the third one was dark, so 
I retreated to Sokoban and collected the bag of holding.  Robbed two shops 
with the old "boulder against door, grab everything and read spellbooks to 
teleport out" trick.  Found speed boots lying around.

The Minetown lighting shop had 3 oil lamps; the toolshop had one blessed 
magic lamp, and many useful tools.  Cashed the lamp in for the Wizard [mode] 
Eye.  Got the luckstone.  Found a rubber chicken, and used that to *ahem* 
get protection from the priest.  Minetown was co-aligned, so I went on a 
sac-spree to restore my luck. 

I had found a ring of conflict, and used my trusty pickaxe to dig from level 
10 all the way to the castle.  There was an Arch-Lich, but I killed him.  
There was a rubber chicken, but I had forgotten to get gloves at Minetown --
luckily a soldier dropped a pair.  The wand was 0:3.

Back to my stash in Sokoban, wished for a spellbook of polymorph and helm of 
brilliance, polypiled spellbooks...





